Consider the problem of determining the extrema of f(x, y) = 2x + y subject to the constraint that √(x) + √(y) = 3. 
We let g(x, y) = √(x) + √(y), so that the Lagrange multiplier equation ∇f(x, y) = λ∇g(x, y), along with the constraint equation, yields the system 

